### MEDUSA API — Administrator Operations & Metrics
### Start API and apply migrations:
### docker compose up --build -d
### docker compose exec api alembic upgrade head
### Use a local account whose database role is admin.
### Never put real production credentials in this file.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1
@adminEmail = admin@example.com
@password = Replace-With-A-Long-Local-Test-Password

### 1. Login as administrator
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{adminEmail}}&password={{password}}

### 2. Read infrastructure and sandbox operational metrics (admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/operations/metrics
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 3. Verify participant access is denied (expected 403)
### Replace token with a participant access token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/operations/metrics
Authorization: Bearer {{participantToken}}


### 4. List persisted operational alert state (admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/operations/alerts?active_only=false&limit=50&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 5. List only currently active alerts
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/operations/alerts?active_only=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 6. Run the scheduled alert evaluator and notification worker manually
### Run from the API project environment / container:
### python -m app.services.operational_alert_worker --batch-size 100
